# School CRM React Project

Production School CRM / School Management SaaS. Admin dashboard style.

## Stack (strict)

- React functional components + hooks only
- React Router, Axios, normal CSS only
- No TypeScript, Tailwind, Bootstrap, MUI, Chakra, styled-components, or CSS frameworks
- No inline styles; separate camelCase CSS files per component

## Naming

- camelCase: files, folders, hooks, CSS, utils, services (e.g. `studentTable.jsx`, `useStudentData.js`)
- PascalCase: React component names (e.g. `StudentTable`)

## Folder structure

```
src/
  assets/{images,icons,fonts}
  theme/          → theme.css (CSS variables), themeColors.js (JS constants)
  apis/
  components/{sidebar,navbar,dashboardCards,common}/ → each: js/, css/, hooks/
  pages/ layouts/ routes/ hooks/ context/ utils/ constants/ services/ data/ styles/
  App.jsx  main.jsx
```

## Theme colors

- All shared colors live in `src/theme/theme.css` and `src/theme/themeColors.js`
- Import `theme/theme.css` once in `main.jsx` (before `global.css`)
- Use `var(--theme-*)` in CSS; use `themeColors` in JS when needed
- Do not hardcode hex values in components — add new tokens to `theme/` first

Component folders: `js/` (components), `css/` (styles), `hooks/` (component-specific hooks).

## Mock data

- All mock/static UI data lives in `src/data/mocks/`
- One folder per area — never hardcode labels, rows, or nav in components:
  - `sidebar/sidebar.mock.js` — brand, menu sections, logout
  - `navbar/navbar.mock.js` — breadcrumbs, search, user profile
  - `dashboard/dashboardPage.mock.js` — dashboard cards, tables, feeds
  - `login/loginPage.mock.js` — login copy and stats
- Export shared entries from `src/data/mocks/index.js`
- Add a new mock file when creating each new screen or layout section

## Sidebar layout

- **Fixed (no scroll):** Scholaris brand + `SCHOOL ERP · V2.4` header, Logout footer
- **Scrollable only:** navigation list between header and footer (`.sidebarNavScroll`)
- Do not include Upgrade to Pro card

## Development

- Reusable components; logic in hooks/services, not UI
- async/await for APIs; loading/error/success states
- API URLs via env vars; modules in `apis/` (e.g. `authApi.js`)
- Tables: pagination, search, filter, responsive scroll, empty/loading states
- Forms: validation, friendly errors, disable submit while loading
- Preserve existing behavior; minimal scope changes; no unnecessary files or renames

## UI

SaaS CRM dashboard: sidebar, navbar, cards, tables, forms. Professional, minimal, soft shadows, rounded corners, responsive media queries. Consistent spacing across modules (Dashboard, Students, Teachers, Attendance, Fees, Timetable, Exams, Results, Notifications, Parent Portal, Settings).

## Priority

Scalability → clean architecture → reusability → responsiveness → maintainability → professional UI → stable functionality.
